  "shorterRoute": "Reuse the proved cusp/lattice integral Hecke word relations and actual rational Tate coordinates to factor the original action. Reuse literal integer coefficient extension, preserving prime values and the same polynomial. Resolve endomorphism instances generically before specializing to the actual nested Tate tensor; no proof limit is increased. Only good-prime adjointness enters the squared annihilator and projector. The native image-idempotent law and already audited restricted-pairing lemma give injectivity on the actual image. Existing original rank-two Hecke coordinates, coefficient specialization and algebraIdempotentLeftIdeal are the next reuse inputs for nonzero two-dimensional image identification.",
  "assumptionsToDischarge": "Original Tate realization of the actual arithmetic primitive idempotent, exact prime and polynomial evaluation, self-adjointness of its actual operator, idempotence of that operator and injectivity of the original coefficient-field pairing on its image. The basis and base point arguments remain the actual upstream coordinate choices, not comparison or nondegeneracy assumptions.",
  "remaining": "The transported projector image must still be proved nonzero and identified with the prescribed two-dimensional specialization. Primitive determinant, residual association, automorphy and all-weight continuation remain open; 16/20, DUB-17--20 OPEN.",
